sburg is its second-largest city and a major cultural centre.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russia","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"RU"},{"title":"Ukraine","extract":"Ukraine is a country in Eastern Europe. It is the second-largest country in Europe after Russia, which borders it to the east and northeast. Ukraine also borders Belarus to the north; Poland and Slovakia to the west; Hungary, Romania and Moldova to the southwest; and the Black Sea and the Sea of Azov to the south and southeast. Kyiv is Ukraine's capital and largest city, followed by Kharkiv, Odesa, and Dnipro. The official language is Ukrainian. Ukraine covers about 600,000 km2 (230,000 sq mi), with around 32 million people.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ukraine","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"UA"}],"arc":{"reports":54,"first_seen":"2026-10-10T06:00:45Z","first_title":"As Russia escalates its war , the EU realises its support for Ukraine wont be enough","first_url":"https://www.euronews.com/2026/10/10/as-russia-escalates-its-war-the-eu-admits-its-support-for-ukraine-wont-be-enough","first_publisher":"euronews.com","earlier":[{"id":"e_9fa59bccccb4","title":"Polish military to practise deploying forces in Ukraine in event of ceasefire with Russia – media","date":"2026-10-17T09:22:00Z","url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","publisher":"Українська правда","verification":"single_source_report"},{"id":"e_4452a7968871","title":"Russia Reports Elimination of Ukrainian Troops in Kharkov Region","date":"2026-10-17T10:00:13Z","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqAFBVV95cUxQUzV1MUdtUl9sYkN6Q0RyMUhVX2ZUckVYQU5LeUg5SVdTMVVHbGgxakV6eEZ6WGhMS2xlVTQ4eDR4Tl84Yi11UXdBcURjQjlKcXUzU1JwTXczRkZsYnBwZjJyWXo2RFkxWXp5ZTdjQndIXzkwS25uZVZmR2NURjA1eHExRFU1eXBaMTVpcXlFN0VucHFMUTB2bFcxNVpLNldLT1hvVWdFYzg?oc=5","publisher":"Военное дело","verification":"single_source_report"},{"id":"e_6fc606f9d360","title":"Ukraine Repels Russia’s Largest Motorcycle Assault of 2026 